   word in the Arabic body contradicts R5 and the checker's `english` lane.
4. b#42 (子女 → 'الطفل') was applied to 016 only, as the row scopes it ("title, FAQ and §§5–8").
   007 also renders 子女 as 'الابن' in ~30 places; neither reviewer flagged it there, and a
   blanket sweep of a file rated "usable legal MSA" was judged out of scope. Recommend a
   follow-up decision by the supervisor if locale-wide consistency is wanted.
5. a#7's suggested imperative ('أضيفوا بعد الجملة…') was rendered as running prose matching the
   English "Country-specific note" sentence rather than as an instruction to the reader.
6. NOT a disagreement, but a gap: a#14 (005 body link to the Hangul Wix slug) and b#4 (011
   Invest Taiwan `lang=jpn`) were marked "already fixed mechanically" in ACCEPTED-ar; they are
   NOT fixed in the tree. Both need an href change, which this lane may not make.

